  body: "# Missing medical evidence and the incapacity decision\n\n## Authored interpretation\n\nWhere
    medical evidence has a gap before incapacity is determined and contact has not been lost, the source
    distinguishes possible payment suspension from the incapacity determination and says the gap alone
    does not justify superseding entitlement.\n\n## Scope and exceptions\n\nDMG 13182–13184 require the
    personal capability assessment and all available evidence in the stated circumstances. Lost contact
    has separate provisions. This is legacy incapacity guidance, not a blanket bar on suspension or a
    present-day ESA/UC decision rule.\n\n## Inspected source passages\n\n- [DMG 13182, PDF page 12](https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/5a74dd8b40f0b65f61322dcd/dmgch13.pdf#page=12)
    — DMG Vol 3 Ch 13: Incapacity for work.\n- [DMG 13183, PDF page 12](https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/5a74dd8b40f0b65f61322dcd/dmgch13.pdf#page=12)
    — DMG Vol 3 Ch 13: Incapacity for work.\n- [DMG 13184, PDF page 12](https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/5a74dd8b40f0b65f61322dcd/dmgch13.pdf#page=12)
    — DMG Vol 3 Ch 13: Incapacity for work.\n\n## Evidence and review status\n\nModel-assisted interpretation
    of selected passages in the 15 September 2026 frozen source snapshot. Specialist review is required.
    Source acquisition, source revision, legal effective dates and this record’s authoring time are separate.\n\
    \nThis is an independent experimental publication, not an official DWP document, individual advice,
    an entitlement decision or an executable rule. Machine-extracted text may alter reading order, footnotes
    and characters. No PDF visual inspection, whole-chapter coverage or behavioural evaluation pass is
    claimed by this record.\n\n- `dmg-vol3-ch13`: PDF SHA-256 `fc4496aae0bb510fea99ee047b82bbb00182dd336af8dfb065ef040f3967078f`;
    extracted pages SHA-256 `1c3e2ae8cf5c3f45273274f24d1bafff88d21a657237c557d555fed53088c931`.\n"
  semantic_relations:
  - target: term/dmg-payment-suspension
    predicate: http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#related
    rationale: The source allows payment suspension in the stated medical-evidence-gap circumstances
      while preserving the separate entitlement determination.
    evidence:
    - page: page/dmg-vol3-ch13/0012
      quote: "13182   If a claimant fails to provide medical evidence for a specific period before incapacity\n\
        \        is determined and contact with them has not been lost, payment of benefit may be\n  \
        \                  1\n        suspended (see DMG Chapter 04 for guidance on suspension of payment
        of\n        benefit).\n                                                                      \
        \       1 SS CS (D&A) Regs, reg 16"
      locator: DMG 13182
  - target: term/dmg-supersession
    predicate: http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#related
    rationale: The source says the lack of a certificate is not itself the change establishing the
      ground; the incapacity determination supplies the relevant basis.
    evidence:
    - page: page/dmg-vol3-ch13/0012
      quote: "13184   Where there is a gap in medical evidence, this does not count as a change of\n \
        \       circumstances to justify a decision to supersede the entitlement decision. The DM\n  \
        \      can suspend payment to the claimant because of the failure to provide medical\n       \
        \ evidence, but cannot conclude they are not entitled to IB without carrying out the\n       \
        \      1\n        PCA . The determination of incapacity for work gives grounds for supersession,
        not\n        the lack of medical evidence. Once incapacity has been determined, any days not\n\
        \        covered by medical evidence will be included in the PCA determination (see DMG\n    \
        \    13622).\n                                                                               \
        \              1 R(IB) 1/05\n\n        Contact with claimant lost"
      locator: DMG 13184
